n value against high-card hands (like K-high) that the opponent might hold. Betting is unlikely to be called by a worse hand (only better hands or strong pairs would call), and checking guarantees I see the showdown for free to potentially win the current pot.\n\nReason:\nI have a made hand (Pair of 3s) with reasonable kickers. Since the opponent has shown no aggression, checking is the optimal play to realize my equity and win against their weak range without risking additional chips on a board with three overcards (A, J, 10).\n\nAnswer: 0'}
