e spades. The opponent checked both the Flop and the Turn, suggesting they likely do not have a strong hand like a flush, straight, or top pair. They likely hold a weak pair or missed draws (air). My hand beats all their air/missed draw combinations. While a bet might bluff them off a weak pair (like a pair of 2s or 3s), it also opens me up to a loss if they call or raise. Since I am already beating a significant portion of their range (their bluffs and air), checking allows me to realize this equity without risking more chips.\n\nReason: I have good showdown value beating all missed draws and high cards. Opponent showed weakness by checking twice. Checking avoids the risk of being bluff-caught by a weak pair while collecting the pot against their air.\n\nAnswer: 0'}
